{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310864,"nonce":"FSrEXrBjG5Jb/Oe/KRNCeoZLLa8=","title":"THE intended snapshot design per the owner: the CLI crate's build.rs lowers the stdlib and embeds it, so there is NO warm-up step","message":"OWNER'S ACTUAL INSTRUCTION, which I misread once (I built a `cache warm`-based\nshared store instead — see [[project_stdlib_prepared_cache_next_steps]]):\n\n\u003e \"make the cli have a build.rs that compiles the snapshot binary with the cli,\n\u003e **so no need for warm up**.\"\n\nThe snapshot ships INSIDE the binary. No install step, no warm command, no\nper-machine preparation. A fresh container is fast on its first run.\n\n**FEASIBILITY IS SETTLED — both blockers I raised were wrong:**\n1. `cargo check -p compiler --no-default-features` **SUCCEEDS in 3m31s**.\n   Lowering needs NO llvm / cranelift / wasm backend, so the build-dependency\n   copy of `compiler` is cheap.\n2. Workspace root Cargo.toml is a package with `edition = \"2021\"`, so\n   **resolver v2** applies and build-dependency features do NOT unify with\n   normal ones — the build-dep copy stays backend-free while the linked copy\n   keeps LLVM.\n3. NO VERSION SKEW, unlike shelling out to an installed binary: build.rs\n   compiles the SAME source tree that gets linked, so MIR layout matches by\n   construction. (This is why CLI-local generation beats a `build.rs` that\n   invokes an external `rayzor`.)\n\n**LANDED ON MAIN 2026-08-15 (`41eff717`). Fresh checkout, no warm step:\n`Sys.println` program 702ms -\u003e 42ms; nbody 31 -\u003e 19ms; mandelbrot 29 -\u003e 16ms,\nall `cache_hit=N cache_miss=0`. Checksum 112798288 unchanged, suite 184/184.**\n\nSHAPE THAT WORKED:\n- `snapshot-gen` — a NORMAL WORKSPACE BINARY (not a build script) that lowers a\n  warm-up program per tier define and writes the archive.\n- root `build.rs` — embeds `target/stdlib_snapshot.bin` (override with\n  `RAYZOR_SNAPSHOT`), or an EMPTY archive when absent so a plain `cargo build`\n  still works and just compiles from source.\n- `src/main.rs` — `snapshot::install(include_bytes!(...))` before anything\n  compiles.\n- Build: `cargo build -p snapshot-gen \u0026\u0026 ./target/release/snapshot-gen\n  target/stdlib_snapshot.bin \u0026\u0026 cargo build -p rayzor`.\n\n**WHY THE GENERATOR CANNOT BE A BUILD SCRIPT** (cost a full cycle): `compiler`\ndepends non-optionally on `rayzor-runtime`, which builds a fixed-name dylib. Any\nbuild-dependency path to `compiler` puts it in the HOST graph beside the target\ngraph's copy; cargo writes both to\n`target/release/deps/librayzor_runtime.dylib` (\"output filename collision\") and\nthe thin-LTO link then fails with `failed to get bitcode from object file for\nLTO (Can't find section __bitcode)`. `[profile.release.build-override]` cannot\ncarry `lto`, so there is no flag-level escape. Keep the generator in the TARGET\ngraph.\n\nHISTORICAL STATUS (superseded):\n\nDONE and committed: `compiler/src/ir/snapshot.rs` (archive format\n`RZSN|count|[len|key|len|data]*`, indexed in place, keys\n`\u003cdiscriminator\u003e/\u003cmodule\u003e.blade`), `load_blade_from_bytes`, and the fallback in\n`try_load_blade_cached_full`. Inert until something installs an archive; suite\n184/184.\n\nPROVEN TO WORK: a root `build.rs` with `[build-dependencies] compiler = { path\n= \"compiler\", default-features = false }` DID generate the archive — **126\nmodules, 640 KB** — and `src/main.rs` installed it via\n`include_bytes!(concat!(env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), \"/stdlib_snapshot.bin\"))`.\n\n**THE BLOCKER (reverted, tree is green without it):** making `compiler` a\nbuild-dependency of the SAME binary pulls `rayzor-runtime` into the host graph.\nCargo then writes host and target copies to the same\n`target/release/deps/librayzor_runtime.dylib` (\"output filename collision\"\nwarnings), and the final thin-LTO link fails with\n`failed to get bitcode from object file for LTO (Can't find section __bitcode)`.\n`[profile.release.build-override]` cannot carry `lto` (cargo rejects it), so\nthat escape hatch is closed. FIX DIRECTION: put the generator in its OWN\nworkspace crate (e.g. `snapshot-gen`) that the build script runs as a separate\nbinary, so the host graph never collides with the target graph.\n\n**SECOND REAL BUG FOUND EN ROUTE (fix verified to compile, then reverted with\nthe rest):** `compiler/build.rs::cache_build_id()` hashes\n`CARGO_FEATURE_LLVM_BACKEND` / `WASM_RUNTIME` / `GPU_RUNTIME`, so a\nbackend-free build-dependency copy gets a DIFFERENT `RAYZOR_BUILD_ID` and every\nartifact it produces is rejected by the linked copy — the load path's build-id\nguard doing its job on a false difference. A `.blade` holds MIR and type info,\nall produced before a backend is chosen, so the id should cover target shape\nonly. Drop those three keys.\n\n**IMPLEMENTATION:**\n- Root `Cargo.toml`: add\n  `[build-dependencies] compiler = { path = \"compiler\", default-features = false }`\n  (the bin crate has NO build.rs today — create `build.rs` at the repo root).\n- `build.rs`: construct a `CompilationUnit` per tier define (`jit`, `llvm`,\n  `interp` — the discriminator follows the defines, see below), `load_stdlib()`,\n  add a warmup program that REACHES `Sys` (an empty `main` lowers almost\n  nothing), `lower_to_tast()`, and serialize the resulting per-module artifacts\n  into `$OUT_DIR`. Emit `cargo:rerun-if-changed=compiler/haxe-std`.\n- Consumer: `include_bytes!(concat!(env!(\"OUT_DIR\"), ...))` and, in\n  `try_load_blade_cached_full` (compiler/src/compilation.rs), fall back to the\n  EMBEDDED set when `blade_cache_path` has no entry — the same seam the\n  prepared-store fallback already uses.\n- Delete the `cache warm`-based prepared store once embedding lands, or demote\n  it to an override.\n\n**HARD-WON DETAILS THAT WILL BITE:**\n- **Discriminator must match the consumer.** `cache_discriminator()` is\n  `native` when `extra_defines` is empty and `native-\u003chash\u003e` otherwise; a real\n  run carries one of `jit`/`llvm`/`interp` (src/main.rs ~1682). Generate for\n  each, or the artifact is written where nothing looks for it.\n- **Size is a non-issue:** 42-module `Sys` closure = 211 KB lowered; binary is\n  223 MB. 126 modules across 3 tiers = 619 KB.\n- Build-id validation already exists in the load path and rejects an artifact\n  from a different compiler, falling back to source. Keep that.\n- Expect a doubled `compiler` compile on clean builds (host copy, backend-free).\n\n**MEASUREMENT THAT PROVES IT:** brand-new project dir, `.rayzor` absent,\n`RAYZOR_PROFILE_TYPECHECK=1 rayzor run --plain S.hx` where S.hx is\n`class S { static function main() { Sys.println(\"x\"); } }`. Want\n`cache_hit=42 cache_miss=0` and compile ~26ms, versus 702ms today. Gate on the\nfull suite (184/184) plus checksum 112798288.\n\nEDITING TRAP, hit TWICE in one session: `src/main.rs` has four identical\n`let mut config = CompilationConfig::default();` lines; a first-match replace\npatches `cache_stats`, not `cache_warm`. Anchor edits on the enclosing `fn`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_stdlib_snapshot_embed_via_cli_buildrs` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}